data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","item":{"id":"mcp_076287ff3bf5a474006aa11820fecc87d0ab063673bc6f4b59","type":"mcp_call","status":"completed","approval_request_id":null,"arguments":"{\"query\":\"Azure OpenAI Service site:learn.microsoft.com\"}","error":null,"name":"microsoft_docs_search","output":"{\"results\": [{\"title\": \"Generate code with Azure OpenAI Service - Training\", \"content\": \"# Generate code with Azure OpenAI Service\\r\\n\\r\\n- Module\\r\\n- 7 Units\\r\\n\\r\\n Intermediate \\r\\n\\r\\n AI Engineer \\r\\n\\r\\n Developer \\r\\n\\r\\n Solution Architect \\r\\n\\r\\n Student \\r\\n\\r\\n Azure OpenAI Service \\r\\n\\r\\n Azure \\r\\n\\r\\nThis module shows engineers how to use the Azure OpenAI Service to generate and improve code.\\r\\n\\r\\n##  Learning objectives \\r\\n\\r\\nBy the end of this module, you'll be able to:\\r\\n\\r\\n- Use natural language prompts to write code\\r\\n- Build unit tests and understand complex code with AI models\\r\\n- Generate comments and documentation for existing code\\r\\n\\r\\n## Prerequisites\\r\\n\\r\\n- Familiarity with Azure and the Azure portal.\\r\\n- An understanding of generative AI. You can learn more with [Introduction to Azure OpenAI Service](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/explore-azure-openai/).\\r\\n- Experience programming with C# or Python. If you have no previous programming experience, we recommend you complete the [Take your first steps with C#](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/paths/csharp-first-steps/) or [Take your first steps with Python](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/paths/python-first-steps/) learning path before starting this one.\\r\\n- Before starting this module, we recommend you complete the previous modules in the [Develop AI solutions with Azure OpenAI](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/paths/develop-ai-solutions-azure-openai/) learning path.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Get started with Azure\\r\\n\\r\\nChoose the Azure account that's right for you. Pay as you go or try Azure free for up to 30 days. [Sign up.](https://azure.microsoft.com/pricing/purchase-options/azure-account?icid=msft_learn)\\r\\n\\r\\nTake the module assessment\\r\\n\\r\\n Module Assessment Results\\r\\n\\r\\nAssess your understanding of this module. Sign in and answer all questions correctly to earn a pass designation on your profile.\\r\\n\\r\\n- [Introduction](https://learn.microsoft.com/training/modules/generate-code-azure-openai/1-introduction)\\r\\n- [Construct code from natural language](https://learn.microsoft.com/training/modules/generate-code-azure-openai/2-construct-code-natural-language)\\r\\n- [Complete code and assist the development process](https://learn.microsoft.com/training/modules/generate-code-azure-openai/3-complete-code-assist-development)\\r\\n- [Fix bugs and improve your code](https://learn.microsoft.com/training/modules/generate-code-azure-openai/4-fix-bugs-improve-code)\\r\\n- [Exercise - Generate and improve code with Azure OpenAI Service](https://learn.microsoft.com/training/modules/generate-code-azure-openai/5-exercise)\\r\\n- [Module assessment](https://learn.microsoft.com/training/modules/generate-code-azure-openai/6-knowledge-check)\\r\\n- [Summary](https://learn.microsoft.com/training/modules/generate-code-azure-openai/7-summary)\\r\\n\\r\\nTake the module assessment\\r\\n\\r\\n Module Assessment Results\\r\\n\\r\\nAssess your understanding of this module. Sign in and answer all questions correctly to earn a pass designation on your profile.\", \"contentUrl\": \"https://learn.microsoft.com/training/modules/generate-code-azure-openai/\"}, {\"title\": \"Build natural language solutions with Azure OpenAI Service - Training\", \"content\": \"# Build natural language solutions with Azure OpenAI Service\\r\\n\\r\\n- Module\\r\\n- 7 Units\\r\\n\\r\\n Intermediate \\r\\n\\r\\n AI Engineer \\r\\n\\r\\n Developer \\r\\n\\r\\n Solution Architect \\r\\n\\r\\n Student \\r\\n\\r\\n Azure OpenAI Service \\r\\n\\r\\n Azure \\r\\n\\r\\nThis module provides engineers with the skills to begin building apps that integrate with the Azure OpenAI Service.\\r\\n\\r\\n##  Learning objectives \\r\\n\\r\\nBy the end of this module, you'll be able to:\\r\\n\\r\\n- Integrate Azure OpenAI into your application\\r\\n- Differentiate between different endpoints available to your application\\r\\n- Generate completions to prompts using the REST API and language specific SDKs\\r\\n\\r\\n## Prerequisites\\r\\n\\r\\n- Familiarity with Azure and the Azure portal.\\r\\n- An understanding of generative AI. You can learn more with [Introduction to Azure OpenAI Service](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/explore-azure-openai/).\\r\\n- Experience programming with C# or Python. If you have no previous programming experience, we recommend you complete the [Take your first steps with C#](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/paths/csharp-first-steps/) or [Take your first steps with Python](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/paths/python-first-steps/) learning path before starting this one.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Get started with Azure\\r\\n\\r\\nChoose the Azure account that's right for you. Pay as you go or try Azure free for up to 30 days. [Sign up.](https://azure.microsoft.com/pricing/purchase-options/azure-account?icid=msft_learn)\\r\\n\\r\\nTake the module assessment\\r\\n\\r\\n Module Assessment Results\\r\\n\\r\\nAssess your understanding of this module. Sign in and answer all questions correctly to earn a pass designation on your profile.\\r\\n\\r\\n- [Introduction](https://learn.microsoft.com/training/modules/build-language-solution-azure-openai/1-introduction)\\r\\n- [Integrate Azure OpenAI into your app](https://learn.microsoft.com/training/modules/build-language-solution-azure-openai/2-integrate-azure-openai-into-app)\\r\\n- [Use Azure OpenAI REST API](https://learn.microsoft.com/training/modules/build-language-solution-azure-openai/3-use-openai-rest)\\r\\n- [Use Azure OpenAI SDK](https://learn.microsoft.com/training/modules/build-language-solution-azure-openai/4-use-openai-sdk)\\r\\n- [Exercise - Integrate Azure OpenAI into your app](https://learn.microsoft.com/training/modules/build-language-solution-azure-openai/5-exercise)\\r\\n- [Module assessment](https://learn.microsoft.com/training/modules/build-language-solution-azure-openai/6-knowledge-check)\\r\\n- [Summary](https://learn.microsoft.com/training/modules/build-language-solution-azure-openai/7-summary)\\r\\n\\r\\nTake the module assessment\\r\\n\\r\\n Module Assessment Results\\r\\n\\r\\nAssess your understanding of this module. Sign in and answer all questions correctly to earn a pass designation on your profile.\", \"contentUrl\": \"https://learn.microsoft.com/training/modules/build-language-solution-azure-openai/\"}, {\"title\": \"AI: Create an Azure OpenAI Resource and Deploy a Model\", \"content\": \"# AI: Create an Azure OpenAI Resource and Deploy a Model\\nTo get started using Azure OpenAI in your applications, you need to create an Azure OpenAI Service and deploy a model that can be used to perform tasks such as converting natural language to SQL, generating email/SMS message content, and more.\\nIn this exercise you will:\\n1. Create an Azure OpenAI Service resource.\\n2. Deploy a model.\\n3. Update the *.env* file with values from your Azure OpenAI service resource.\\n![Microsoft Cloud scenario overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/microsoft-cloud/dev/tutorials/openai-acs-msgraph/media/scenario-overview-no-title.png)\\n### Create an Azure OpenAI Service Resource\\n1. Visit the [Azure portal](https://portal.azure.com) in your browser and sign in.\\n2. Enter *openai* in the **search bar** at the top of the portal page and select **Azure OpenAI** from the options that appear.\\n ![Azure OpenAI Service in the Azure portal](https://learn.microsoft.com/microsoft-cloud/dev/tutorials/openai-acs-msgraph/media/search-openai-portal.png)\\n3. Select **Create** in the toolbar.\\n Note\\n While this tutorial focuses on Azure OpenAI, if you have an OpenAI API key and would like to use it, you can skip this section and go directly to the **Update the Project's .env File** section below. Assign your OpenAI API key to `OPENAI_API_KEY` in the *.env* file (you can ignore any other `.env` instructions related to OpenAI).\\n4. Azure OpenAI models are available in specific regions. Visit the [Azure OpenAI model availability](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/ai-services/openai/concepts/models?WT.mc_id=m365-94501-dwahlin#global-standard-model-availability) document to learn which regions support the gpt-4o model used in this tutorial.\\n5. Perform the following tasks:\\n5.1. Select your Azure subscription.\\n5.2. Select the resource group to use (create a new one if needed).\\n5.3. Select a region where the gpt-4o model is supported based on the document you looked at earlier.\\n5.4. Enter the resource name. It must be a unique value.\\n5.5. Select the **Standard S0** pricing tier.\\n6. Select **Next** until you get to the **Review + submit** screen. Select **Create**.\\n7. Once your Azure OpenAI resource is created, navigate to it and select **Resource Management** --> **Keys and Endpoint** .\", \"contentUrl\": \"https://learn.microsoft.com/microsoft-cloud/dev/tutorials/openai-acs-msgraph/02-openai-create-resource\"}, {\"title\": \"Develop applications with Azure OpenAI in Foundry Models - Training\", \"content\": \"# Develop applications with Azure OpenAI in Foundry Models\\r\\n\\r\\n- Module\\r\\n- 9 Units\\r\\n\\r\\n Intermediate \\r\\n\\r\\n AI Engineer \\r\\n\\r\\n Developer \\r\\n\\r\\n Solution Architect \\r\\n\\r\\n Student \\r\\n\\r\\n Azure OpenAI Service \\r\\n\\r\\n Azure \\r\\n\\r\\nThis module provides engineers with the skills to begin building an Azure OpenAI solution.\\r\\n\\r\\n##  Learning objectives \\r\\n\\r\\nBy the end of this module, you'll be able to:\\r\\n\\r\\n- Create an Azure OpenAI resource and understand types of Azure OpenAI base models.\\r\\n- Build natural language solutions with Azure OpenAI\\r\\n- Apply prompt engineering with Azure OpenAI\\r\\n- Build code-generation solutions with Azure OpenAI\\r\\n\\r\\n## Prerequisites\\r\\n\\r\\n- Familiarity with Azure and the Azure portal.\\r\\n- An understanding of generative AI. You can learn more with [Introduction to Azure OpenAI](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/explore-azure-openai/).\\r\\n\\r\\n## Get started with Azure\\r\\n\\r\\nChoose the Azure account that's right for you. Pay as you go or try Azure free for up to 30 days. [Sign up.](https://azure.microsoft.com/pricing/purchase-options/azure-account?icid=msft_learn)\\r\\n\\r\\nTake the module assessment\\r\\n\\r\\n Module Assessment Results\\r\\n\\r\\nAssess your understanding of this module. Sign in and answer all questions correctly to earn a pass designation on your profile.\\r\\n\\r\\n- [Introduction](https://learn.microsoft.com/training/modules/develop-applications-openai/1-introduction)\\r\\n- [Access Azure OpenAI in Foundry Models](https://learn.microsoft.com/training/modules/develop-applications-openai/2-getting-started)\\r\\n- [Integrate OpenAI into an app](https://learn.microsoft.com/training/modules/develop-applications-openai/3-integrate-app)\\r\\n- [OpenAI prompt engineering](https://learn.microsoft.com/training/modules/develop-applications-openai/4-prompt-engineering)\\r\\n- [Provide context with prompt engineering](https://learn.microsoft.com/training/modules/develop-applications-openai/5-prompt-engineering-provide-context)\\r\\n- [Construct code from natural language](https://learn.microsoft.com/training/modules/develop-applications-openai/6-generating-code)\\r\\n- [Exercise - Get started with Azure OpenAI](https://learn.microsoft.com/training/modules/develop-applications-openai/7-exercise)\\r\\n- [Module assessment](https://learn.microsoft.com/training/modules/develop-applications-openai/8-knowledge-check)\\r\\n- [Summary](https://learn.microsoft.com/training/modules/develop-applications-openai/9-summary)\\r\\n\\r\\nTake the module assessment\\r\\n\\r\\n Module Assessment Results\\r\\n\\r\\nAssess your understanding of this module. Sign in and answer all questions correctly to earn a pass designation on your profile.\", \"contentUrl\": \"https://learn.microsoft.com/training/modules/develop-applications-openai/\"}, {\"title\": \"What is Azure OpenAI in Azure AI Foundry Models?\", \"content\": \"# What is Azure OpenAI in Azure AI Foundry Models?\\n## Get started with Azure OpenAI\\nTo get started with Azure OpenAI, you need to create an Azure OpenAI resource in your Azure subscription.\\nStart with the [Create and deploy an Azure OpenAI resource](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/ai-foundry/openai/how-to/create-resource) guide.\\n1. You can create a resource via Azure portal, Azure CLI, or Azure PowerShell.\\n2. When you have an Azure OpenAI resource, you can deploy a model such as GPT-4o.\\n3. When you have a deployed model, you can:\\n3.1. Try out the [Azure AI Foundry portal](https://ai.azure.com/?cid=learnDocs) playgrounds to explore the capabilities of the models.\\n3.2. You can also just start making API calls to the service using the REST API or SDKs.\\nFor example, you can try [real-time audio](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/ai-foundry/openai/realtime-audio-quickstart) in the playgrounds or via code.\\nNote\\nA Limited Access registration form is required to access some Azure OpenAI models or features. Learn more on the [Azure OpenAI Limited Access page](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/ai-foundry/responsible-ai/openai/limited-access).\\n## Comparing Azure OpenAI and OpenAI\\nAzure OpenAI gives customers advanced language AI with OpenAI GPT-4, GPT-3, Codex, GPT-image-1 (preview), DALL-E, speech to text, and text to speech models with the security and enterprise promise of Azure. Azure OpenAI co-develops the APIs with OpenAI, ensuring compatibility and a smooth transition from one to the other.\\nWith Azure OpenAI, customers get the security capabilities of Microsoft Azure while running the same models as OpenAI. Azure OpenAI offers private networking, regional availability, and responsible AI content filtering.\", \"contentUrl\": \"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/ai-foundry/openai/overview#get-started-with-azure-openai\"}, {\"title\": \"Create and deploy an Azure OpenAI in Azure AI Foundry Models resource (web-portal)\", \"content\": \"# Create and deploy an Azure OpenAI in Azure AI Foundry Models resource (web-portal)\\nThis article describes how to get started with Azure OpenAI and provides step-by-step instructions to create a resource and deploy a model. You can create resources in Azure in several different ways:\\n1. The [Azure portal](https://portal.azure.com/?microsoft_azure_marketplace_ItemHideKey=microsoft_openai_tip#create/Microsoft.CognitiveServicesOpenAI)\\n2. The REST APIs, the Azure CLI, PowerShell, or client libraries\\n3. Azure Resource Manager (ARM) templates\\nIn this article, you review examples for creating and deploying resources in the Azure portal and with the Azure CLI.\\n## Prerequisites\\n1. An Azure subscription. [Create one for free](https://azure.microsoft.com/free/ai-services).\\n2. Access permissions to [create Azure OpenAI resources and to deploy models](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/ai-foundry/openai/how-to/role-based-access-control).\", \"contentUrl\": \"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/ai-foundry/openai/how-to/create-resource\"}, {\"title\": \"Tutorial: Build a chatbot with Azure App Service and Azure OpenAI (.NET)\", \"content\": \"# Tutorial: Build a chatbot with Azure App Service and Azure OpenAI (.NET)\\n## 1. Create an Azure OpenAI resource\\nIn this section, you use Azure CLI in GitHub Codespaces to create an Azure OpenAI resource.\\n1. Sign in to [GitHub Codespaces](https://github.com/codespaces) with your GitHub account.\\n2. Select **Use this template** in the **Blank** tile to create a new blank codespace.\\n3. In the Codespace terminal, install the Azure CLI.\\n```bash\\n curl -sL https://aka.ms/InstallAzureCLIDeb | sudo bash\\n```\\n4. Sign in to your Azure account.\\n```azurecli\\n az login\\n```\\n Follow the instructions in the terminal to authenticate.\\n5. Set environment variables by providing names for your resource group and Azure OpenAI service and setting an appropriate Azure region as your location.\\n```azurecli\\n export RESOURCE_GROUP=\\\"<group-name>\\\"\\n export OPENAI_SERVICE_NAME=\\\"<azure-openai-name>\\\"\\n export APPSERVICE_NAME=\\\"<app-name>\\\"\\n export LOCATION=\\\"<azure-region>\\\"\\n```\\n Important\\n The location is tied to the regional availability of the chosen model. Model and [deployment type](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/ai-foundry/foundry-models/concepts/deployment-types) availability vary among Azure regions and billing tiers. This tutorial uses `gpt-4o-mini`, which is available in several regions under the Standard deployment type.\\n Before selecting a location, consult the [Model summary and region availability table](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/ai-services/openai/concepts/models#model-summary-table-and-region-availability) to verify model support in your preferred region.\\n6. Create a resource group and an Azure OpenAI resource with a custom domain, and then add a `gpt-4o-mini` model:\\nNow that you have an Azure OpenAI resource, you can create a web application to interact with it.\", \"contentUrl\": \"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/app-service/tutorial-ai-openai-chatbot-dotnet#1-create-an-azure-openai-resource\"}, {\"title\": \"Transparency note for Azure OpenAI\", \"content\": \"# Transparency note for Azure OpenAI\\n## Learn more about Azure OpenAI\\n1. [Limited access to Azure OpenAI Service - Foundry Tools | Microsoft Learn](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/ai-foundry/responsible-ai/openai/limited-access)\\n2. [Code of Conduct for the Azure OpenAI Service | Microsoft Learn](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/legal/ai-code-of-conduct?context=%2Fazure%2Fcognitive-services%2Fopenai%2Fcontext%2Fcontext)\\n3. [Data, privacy, and security for Azure OpenAI Service - Foundry Tools | Microsoft Learn](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/ai-foundry/responsible-ai/openai/data-privacy)\", \"contentUrl\": \"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/foundry/responsible-ai/openai/transparency-note#learn-more-about-azure-openai\"}, {\"title\": \"Tutorial: Build a chatbot with Azure App Service and Azure OpenAI (Flask)\", \"content\": \"# Tutorial: Build a chatbot with Azure App Service and Azure OpenAI (Flask)\\nIn this tutorial, you build an intelligent AI application by integrating Azure OpenAI with a Python web application and deploy it to Azure App Service. You create a Flask app that sends chat completion requests to a model in Azure OpenAI, and connect to the service using a managed identity.\\nYou learn how to:\\n1. Create an Azure OpenAI resource and deploy a language model.\\n2. Build a Flask application that connects to Azure OpenAI.\\n3. Deploy the application to Azure App Service.\\n4. Implement passwordless secure authentication in the development environment and in Azure.\\n![Screenshot showing a chatbot running in Azure App Service.](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/app-service/media/tutorial-ai-openai-chatbot-python/chat-in-browser.png)\\n## Prerequisites\\n1. An [Azure account](https://azure.microsoft.com/pricing/purchase-options/azure-account?cid=msft_learn) with an active subscription\\n2. A [GitHub account](https://github.com/join) for using GitHub Codespaces\", \"contentUrl\": \"https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/app-service/tutorial-ai-openai-chatbot-python\"}, {\"title\": \"Microsoft Applied Skills: Develop generative AI solutions with Azure OpenAI Service - Applied Skills\", \"content\": \"Applied Skills \\r\\n\\r\\n# Microsoft Applied Skills: Develop generative AI solutions with Azure OpenAI Service\\r\\n\\r\\n Validate your technical skills and open doors to new possibilities of advancement with Microsoft Applied Skills. \\r\\n\\r\\n##  At a glance\\r\\n\\r\\n- Level \\r\\n\\r\\n[Intermediate](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/credentials/browse/?levels=intermediate&amp;credential_types=applied%20skills)\\r\\n- Product \\r\\n\\r\\n[Azure](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/credentials/browse/?products=azure&amp;credential_types=applied%20skills)[Azure OpenAI Service](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/credentials/browse/?products=azure-openai&amp;credential_types=applied%20skills)\\r\\n- Role \\r\\n\\r\\n[AI Engineer](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/credentials/browse/?roles=ai-engineer&amp;credential_types=applied%20skills)[App Maker](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/credentials/browse/?roles=maker&amp;credential_types=applied%20skills)[Developer](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/credentials/browse/?roles=developer&amp;credential_types=applied%20skills)\\r\\n- Subject \\r\\n\\r\\n[Artificial intelligence](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/credentials/browse/?subjects=artificial-intelligence&amp;credential_types=applied%20skills)\\r\\n\\r\\n## Overview\\r\\n\\r\\nWarning\\r\\n\\r\\nThis Applied Skills assessment has been retired. [Explore other Applied Skills](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/credentials/browse/?credential_types=applied%20skills) to keep building your skills.\\r\\n\\r\\nTo earn this Microsoft Applied Skills credential, learners demonstrate the ability to develop generative AI solutions with Azure OpenAI Service.\\r\\n\\r\\nCandidates for this credential should be familiar with Azure services and have experience developing applications by using C# or Python.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Skills earned upon completion\\r\\n\\r\\n- Loading...\\r\\n- Loading...\\r\\n- Loading...\", \"contentUrl\": \"https://learn.microsoft.com/credentials/applied-skills/develop-generative-ai-solutions-with-azure-openai-service/\"}]}","server_label":"microsoft-learn"},"output_index":2,"sequence_number":13}

